<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:04:16 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>为什么克劳德·莫奈一遍又一遍地画同样的场景？这位印象派艺术家痴迷于捕捉时间的转瞬即逝的本质</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-did-claude-monet-paint-the-same-scenes-over-and-over-again-the-impressionist-artist-was-obsessed-with-capturing-the-fleeting-nature-of-time-180989563/</link><description>泰特现代美术馆即将举办的展览将展出莫奈在 1870 年代至 1920 年代创作的 60 多件艺术作品。这些作品揭示了他如何记录不断变化的光线和天气条件</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:01:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-did-claude-monet-paint-the-same-scenes-over-and-over-again-the-impressionist-artist-was-obsessed-with-capturing-the-fleeting-nature-of-time-180989563/</guid></item><item><title>科学家表示，“超级”厄尔尼诺现象带来的酷热天气可能会在二月份导致近50万人死亡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-scorching-temperatures-brought-on-by-the-super-el-nino-could-kill-nearly-half-a-million-people-by-february-180989555/</link><description>预测数字包括六月以来的死亡人数，可能低估了总死亡人数。炎热天气可能会持续到二月之后，气候变化可能会带来其他危及生命的情况，包括洪水、野火和传染病</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-scorching-temperatures-brought-on-by-the-super-el-nino-could-kill-nearly-half-a-million-people-by-february-180989555/</guid></item><item><title>一位金属探测器在德国勘探时惊讶地发现了大量罗马硬币</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-metal-detectorist-exploring-a-field-in-germany-was-stunned-to-discover-a-massive-hoard-of-roman-coins-180989561/</link><description>943 枚第纳尔银币跨越了从公元前 148 年到公元 124 或 125 年近 300 年的罗马历史</description><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-metal-detectorist-exploring-a-field-in-germany-was-stunned-to-discover-a-massive-hoard-of-roman-coins-180989561/</guid></item><item><title>这幅来源神秘的立体派绘画在芝加哥艺术博物馆悬挂了数十年。现在，博物馆将把它归还给合法的犹太继承人</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-cubist-painting-with-a-mysterious-provenance-hung-in-the-art-institute-of-chicago-for-decades-now-the-museum-will-return-it-to-its-rightful-jewish-heirs-180989553/</link><description>红外成像将 20 世纪 Jean Metzinger 的作品与一位收藏家联系起来，该收藏家的作品在二战期间被纳粹命令强制拍卖</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:18:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-cubist-painting-with-a-mysterious-provenance-hung-in-the-art-institute-of-chicago-for-decades-now-the-museum-will-return-it-to-its-rightful-jewish-heirs-180989553/</guid></item><item><title>土耳其研究人员出土了一块刻有世界上最古老和平条约的古代碎片</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-in-turkey-have-unearthed-an-ancient-fragment-inscribed-with-the-worlds-oldest-peace-treaty-180989554/</link><description>这块泥板刻有阿卡德楔形文字，其文字属于古埃及人和赫梯人于公元前 13 世纪签订的《卡迭石和平条约》</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:39:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/researchers-in-turkey-have-unearthed-an-ancient-fragment-inscribed-with-the-worlds-oldest-peace-treaty-180989554/</guid></item><item><title>一只水獭百年来首次回到纽约市布朗克斯河。现在，您可以帮忙命名</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-otter-just-returned-to-new-york-citys-bronx-river-for-the-first-time-in-a-century-now-you-can-help-name-it-180989556/</link><description>今年夏天早些时候，一台追踪相机拍摄了这只动物，这提供了一个充满希望的迹象，表明经过数十年的修复工作，曾经被污染的城市水道正在恢复</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:06:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-otter-just-returned-to-new-york-citys-bronx-river-for-the-first-time-in-a-century-now-you-can-help-name-it-180989556/</guid></item><item><title>科学表明，从促进心理健康到降低痴呆风险，这就是为什么阅读对你非常有益</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-boosting-mental-health-to-reducing-dementia-risk-heres-why-reading-is-extremely-good-for-you-according-to-science-180989548/</link><description>越来越多的证据表明，经常读书可以改善大脑和心理健康，提高读写能力和数学技能，甚至可以减缓认知能力下降。更重要的是，小说似乎还有一个额外的好处，那就是向读者介绍他人的观点</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:33:51 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/from-boosting-mental-health-to-reducing-dementia-risk-heres-why-reading-is-extremely-good-for-you-according-to-science-180989548/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下澳大利亚的“泡泡”海豚，它会追逐鱼直到它们呕吐，然后吃掉它们吐出来的食物</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-bubbles-a-dolphin-in-australia-that-chases-fish-until-they-barf-then-eats-their-upchucked-meals-180989547/</link><description>科学家记录了 11 次 Bubbles 成功以这种方式吃零食的例子。它们标志着对鲸目动物盗窃食物行为的一些首次详细观察，鲸目动物是海洋哺乳动物，包括海豚、鲸鱼和鼠海豚</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-bubbles-a-dolphin-in-australia-that-chases-fish-until-they-barf-then-eats-their-upchucked-meals-180989547/</guid></item><item><title>通过年度鸟类摄影师大赛的 11 张获奖照片体验鸟类的奇妙</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/experience-the-wonder-of-birds-with-these-11-winning-photos-from-the-bird-photographer-of-the-year-contest-180989552/</link><description>从进行交配表演的大鼠尾草到做鬼脸的黄褐色蛙口，这些照片捕捉到了世界鸟类令人惊叹的多样性</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:22:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/experience-the-wonder-of-birds-with-these-11-winning-photos-from-the-bird-photographer-of-the-year-contest-180989552/</guid></item><item><title>这位生活在 14 世纪中国的妇女可能因盗窃或通奸而被割掉鼻子</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-woman-who-lived-in-imperial-china-may-have-had-her-nose-cut-off-as-punishment-for-theft-or-adultery-180989551/</link><description>研究人员在她 700 年前的头骨上发现了愈合的迹象，这表明她在痛苦的制裁中幸存下来，甚至可能继续佩戴假肢</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:30:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-woman-who-lived-in-imperial-china-may-have-had-her-nose-cut-off-as-punishment-for-theft-or-adultery-180989551/</guid></item><item><title>水星有皱纹，表明它正在收缩。现在，科学家表示，地球的萎缩程度远远超出了之前的想象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mercury-has-wrinkles-that-show-its-shrinking-now-scientists-say-the-planet-has-shriveled-far-more-than-we-previously-thought-180989532/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，太阳系最小的行星自大约 45 亿年前诞生以来，已经缩小了 30%</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:12:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/mercury-has-wrinkles-that-show-its-shrinking-now-scientists-say-the-planet-has-shriveled-far-more-than-we-previously-thought-180989532/</guid></item><item><title>克劳德·莫奈长期隐藏的《鸢尾花》即将成为法国有史以来拍卖的最昂贵的画作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/claude-monets-long-hidden-iris-is-about-to-become-the-most-expensive-painting-ever-auctioned-in-france-180989546/</link><description>该艺术品反映了著名印象派后来的抽象风格。苏富比估计这幅画将以 2500 万至 3400 万美元的价格出售</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:12:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/claude-monets-long-hidden-iris-is-about-to-become-the-most-expensive-painting-ever-auctioned-in-france-180989546/</guid></item><item><title>超过80万只蜜蜂在澳大利亚北部的“复杂”抢劫中被盗，价值数万澳元</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/more-than-800000-bees-worth-tens-of-thousands-of-dollars-have-been-stolen-in-sophisticated-heists-across-northern-australia-180989545/</link><description>专家推测，最近一种杀死蜜蜂的寄生虫的传播导致了明目张胆的盗窃行为的增加</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:38:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/more-than-800000-bees-worth-tens-of-thousands-of-dollars-have-been-stolen-in-sophisticated-heists-across-northern-australia-180989545/</guid></item><item><title>科学家称人脑可能由两个不同的神经系统挤压在一起组成</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-the-human-brain-might-be-made-of-two-distinct-nervous-systems-that-got-squished-together-180989539/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，两种不同类型的祖细胞产生器官的正面和背面。这些发现可以帮助研究人员研究影响后脑的人类疾病，因为以前在实验室中制造后脑的神经细胞即使不是不可能，也很困难</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:54:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-say-the-human-brain-might-be-made-of-two-distinct-nervous-systems-that-got-squished-together-180989539/</guid></item><item><title>摄像机捕捉到成年黑猩猩将工具和知识传授给幼崽，向下一代传授重要技能</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/cameras-capture-adult-chimpanzees-passing-tools-and-know-how-to-their-young-teaching-important-skills-to-the-next-generation-180989538/</link><description>研究人员录制了塞内加尔野生黑猩猩的视频，向年轻人展示如何用棍子捞出蚂蚁，以及如何用石头砸碎猴面包树果实来打开它，以及其他指导实例</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/cameras-capture-adult-chimpanzees-passing-tools-and-know-how-to-their-young-teaching-important-skills-to-the-next-generation-180989538/</guid></item><item><title>工人们从多瑙河中挖出砾石，挖出了一件拥有 2200 年历史的“生锈宝藏”，该宝藏原本可以装备一支军队</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/workers-excavating-gravel-from-the-danube-river-dredged-up-a-2200-year-old-rusty-treasure-that-could-have-equipped-an-army-180989542/</link><description>缓存中至少有 500 根铁条的残骸，这些铁条很可能被送往下游锻造成成品</description><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/workers-excavating-gravel-from-the-danube-river-dredged-up-a-2200-year-old-rusty-treasure-that-could-have-equipped-an-army-180989542/</guid></item><item><title>一本详细描述特诺奇蒂特兰城兴衰的罕见阿兹特克手抄本近两个世纪以来首次回归墨西哥</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-rare-aztec-codex-detailing-the-rise-and-fall-of-tenochtitlan-returns-to-mexico-for-the-first-time-in-nearly-two-centuries-180989536/</link><description>这件文物是阿兹特克历史上最珍贵的视觉记录之一，将在墨西哥城展出三个月</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:34:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-rare-aztec-codex-detailing-the-rise-and-fall-of-tenochtitlan-returns-to-mexico-for-the-first-time-in-nearly-two-centuries-180989536/</guid></item><item><title>亨利八世在英国宗教改革期间依靠这位朝臣来执行他的命令。在幕后，都铎政治家通过秘密保存天主教文本来反抗他的国王</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/henry-viii-relied-on-this-courtier-to-enforce-his-orders-during-the-english-reformation-behind-the-scenes-the-tudor-politician-defied-his-king-by-secretly-saving-a-catholic-text-180989541/</link><description>一份新发现的碎片表明，约翰·盖奇保存了一份 15 世纪的宗教手稿，“当他打算销毁像这本书一样的书籍时，它保持了安全”</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:08:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/henry-viii-relied-on-this-courtier-to-enforce-his-orders-during-the-english-reformation-behind-the-scenes-the-tudor-politician-defied-his-king-by-secretly-saving-a-catholic-text-180989541/</guid></item><item><title>随着年龄的增长和重大转变，大脑会萎缩。但令人惊讶的是，更年期期间似乎不再需要重新布线</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-brain-shrinks-as-we-age-and-during-major-transitions-but-surprisingly-it-seems-to-take-a-break-from-rewiring-during-menopause-180989527/</link><description>青春期、怀孕和更年期是女性大脑的三个主要荷尔蒙转变。研究人员已经知道，在前两个过程中，器官会根据荷尔蒙的变化进行自我调整，但他们还不确定第三个过程</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:51:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-brain-shrinks-as-we-age-and-during-major-transitions-but-surprisingly-it-seems-to-take-a-break-from-rewiring-during-menopause-180989527/</guid></item><item><title>在俄亥俄州发现的犰狳是装甲动物向北扩张的最新惊喜。他们现在在哪里，是什么推动了他们的行动？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-armadillo-found-in-ohio-is-the-latest-surprise-in-the-armored-animals-expansion-north-where-are-they-now-and-whats-driving-their-movement-180989530/</link><description>这些生物通常出现在南部和东南部，随着冬季变得温和，这些生物已经到达越来越远的州，如北卡罗来纳州、弗吉尼亚州和伊利诺伊州</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:56:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-armadillo-found-in-ohio-is-the-latest-surprise-in-the-armored-animals-expansion-north-where-are-they-now-and-whats-driving-their-movement-180989530/</guid></item></channel></rss>